cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "USearch: One Proximity Graph for Search, Sparse Products & Attention across RAM, VRAM & NVMe"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/USearch
url: https://www.unum.cloud/docs/usearch
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.7949415
abstract: >-
  USearch is an open-source proximity-graph index for nearest-neighbor search over dense vectors,
  sequences, shapes and geospatial sets. The same graph serves as a sparse operand, folding sparse
  matrix products, late-interaction MaxSim scoring and softmax attention into its traversal, and
  one checkpoint opens in RAM, on NVMe drives, or in the VRAM of NVIDIA, AMD and Apple GPUs without
  being rewritten. Its core is a header-only C++ 20 library with no external dependencies, and
  ClickHouse, DuckDB, ScyllaDB and YugabyteDB embed it for vector search.
keywords:
  - nearest-neighbor search
  - vector search
  - similarity search
  - sequence search
  - edit distance
  - shape search
  - point clouds
  - geospatial search
  - proximity graph
  - sparse matrix multiplication
  - attention
  - ram
  - vram
  - nvme
  - gpu

